[[Supportive care]]

Topic outline: care during and after cancer treatment, including long-term health and quality of life.

!! Follow-up planning
* Treatment summary and survivorship care plan.
* Disease-specific recurrence surveillance.
* Coordination between oncology, primary care, and other specialists.

!! Late and persistent effects
* Cardiovascular, pulmonary, endocrine, and neurologic effects.
* Bone health, fatigue, pain, sleep, and cognitive concerns.
* Secondary malignancies and treatment exposure-related screening.

!! Health maintenance
* Preventive screening, vaccination, and chronic disease management.
* Physical activity, nutrition, and tobacco cessation.

!! Quality of life
* Fertility, sexual health, and menopausal symptoms.
* Distress, fear of recurrence, and psychosocial support.
* Employment, financial concerns, and caregiver needs.

